{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-161655",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{12-2x-2y}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[z]_{z=1}^{z=12-2x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}12-2x-2y-1\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}11-2x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[11y-2xy-{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}44-8x-16\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-8x+28\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{2}+28x]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =-4+28-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
